  "text": "\"Independent\" is a big word that sounds bigger than it is. When people picture AI acting on its own, they imagine something wandering off, making its own plans. That's not really it.\n\nThink of a thermostat. It acts without you. But only within a range you set. Nobody worries the thermostat will suddenly renovate the kitchen.\n\nMost AI at work is like that. It moves inside a fence someone drew. The real question is: who drew the fence?",
